details:
(a) the State-wise amount sanctioned and utilised from the Nirbhaya Fund during Financial Year 2025-26;
(b) the number of One Stop Centres and Women Helplines strengthened or made functional through this Fund during the said period;
(c) the number of States where additional safety infrastructure projects have been approved under the Fund; and
(d) the additional steps being taken to expedite utilisation of the Fund for women's safety and protection schemes?

(a) whether the Ministry has unveiled 'PRAHAAR' as India's first comprehensive 'National Counter-Terrorism Policy and Strategy,' and if so, the date of unveiling and the key pillars thereof;
(b) the specific objectives of 'PRAHAAR' that could not be effectively addressed under the existing counter-terrorism and internal security framework;
(c) the institutional and coordination mechanisms proposed between Central and State agencies for the implementation of this policy; and
(d) the timeline for the operationalization of this strategy and the manner in which the outcomes thereof would be reviewed?

(a) the steps taken to strengthen collaboration with industry and technology companies to provide industry-relevant skill training;
(b) whether Government has undertaken measures to promote apprenticeship training under the National Apprenticeship Promotion Scheme (NAPS), if so, the details thereof;
(c) whether Direct Benefit Transfer (DBT) support is being provided to apprentices under NAPS-2, if so, the details thereof; and
(d) the special initiatives taken to improve participation of women in apprenticeship training and expand apprenticeship opportunities across service sectors, if so, the details thereof?

(a) the status of the implementation of digital toll collection initiatives on the National Highways;
(b) the information regarding measures undertaken to facilitate technology-enabled toll collection on the National Highway network;
(c) whether the Ministry is planning to expand barrier-free electronic toll collection; and
(d) if so, the details thereof?

(a) the total quantum of Rural Local Body (RLB) Grants recommended by the Sixteenth Finance Commission for Panchayati Raj Institutions during the award period 2026-31, including Chhattisgarh;
(b) the operational guidelines issued for utilisation of these grants and the priority sectors identified for their deployment;
(c) the strategies being adopted to enhance Panchayats' Own Source Revenue (OSR) mobilisation as discussed at the National Workshop held on 3rd July, 2026; and
(d) the mechanism put in place to monitor effective and timely utilisation of Finance Commission grants by States and Panchayati Raj Institutions in Chhattisgarh?

(a) the details of measures taken by Government to develop lighthouses as tourist destinations;
(b) the details of facilities developed at existing lighthouses under the lighthouse tourism initiative;
(c) the details of legislative framework available to support lighthouse tourism and heritage conservation in the country; and
(d) the details of initiatives proposed under the development of lighthouse tourism circuits to promote regional tourism and economic development?

(a) the salient features of the revised Operational Guidelines issued under the Anemia Mukt Bharat Abhiyaan;
(b) the details of the 7×7×7 framework introduced under the revised Operational Guidelines;
(c) the details of the T4 strategy adopted under the scheme for strengthening screening, treatment and follow-up of beneficiaries; and
(d) the details of the unified Anemia Mukt Bharat Abhiyaan Portal and the manner in which it is proposed to strengthen digital tracking and monitoring of anemia services?

(a) whether the fund flow mechanism has improved with the implementation of the Treasury Single Account, Single Nodal Agency, Central Nodal Agency, and SNA SPARSH;
(b) if so, the details thereof;
(c) the details of the measures taken to reduce idle funds through the Treasury Single Account, Single Nodal Agency, Central Nodal Agency, and SNA SPARSH; and
(d) the details of the savings achieved through the aforementioned schemes?

(a) the salient features of the amendments made to Schedule VII to the Companies Act, 2013 to facilitate Corporate Social Responsibility (CSR) through zero coupon zero principal instruments;
(b) the framework prescribed for the implementation of CSR through zero coupon zero principal instruments;
(c) the details of the amendments made to the Companies CSR Rules, 2014 for the implementation of CSR through zero coupon zero principal instruments; and
(d) the details of limits prescribed on the expenditure incurred by companies on CSR through zero coupon zero principal instruments?

(a) the details of measures taken by Government to promote balanced use of fertilizers;
(b) whether any assistance has been provided for the promotion of organic, bio and city-compost fertilizers during the last three years; 
(c) if so, the details thereof; and
(d) the measures taken to promote soil-test-based and crop-specific application of fertilizers?

(a) the details of the specific strategies being implemented by Government through summits to provide global recognition and access to international markets for Geographical Indication (GI) tagged Indian handloom products;
(b) whether Government aims to implement special measures to take GI-tagged handloom products from local markets to global platforms; and
(c) if so, the details thereof?

(a) the details of the infrastructure upgradation and beautification works carried out at railway stations under the Amrit Bharat Station Scheme (ABSS);
(b) whether necessary facilities have been provided to ensure accessibility for passengers with reduced mobility;
(c) if so, the details thereof; and
(d) the number of stations where work has been completed so far, compared to the total number of stations approved under the Scheme, State-wise?

(a) whether community radio stations are being integrated with district-level disaster management and emergency communication plans;
(b) if so, the details thereof;
(c) whether provision has been made to provide backup power arrangements and emergency protocols for these community radio stations; and
(d) if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether Government has approved the National Mission on Edible Oils–Oil Palm (NMEO–OP) with the objective of increasing oilseeds production in the country and achieving self-reliance in edible oils;
(b) if so, the details of the Mission, its objectives/targets, timeline for its implementation and funds released to all States thereunder;
(c) the total budget allocated for NMEO–OP for the period from 2024-25 to 2030-31; and
(d) the additional steps taken/proposed to be taken by Government to promote indigenous oilseeds varieties, reduce dependence on imported hybrid seeds and make the country self-reliant in oilseeds production?

(a) how digital pension platforms like Bhavishya, Digital Life Certificate and CPENGRAMS have improved transparency and timely benefit disbursement for Central Government employees;
(b) whether AI tools for automated grievance sorting and a revised appellate framework have been introduced to reduce pendency and improve responsiveness;
(c) if so, the details thereof; and
(d) the roadmap to merge these platforms into a unified, pensioner-centric system and steps to assist digitally illiterate beneficiaries?

(a) the number of cases taken up and disposed of through e-Lok Adalats during the last three years, State-wise and year wise;
(b) the total amount of monetary settlement arrived through e-Lok Adalats during the said period;
(c) the States/Union Territories where e-Lok Adalats have been introduced or expanded during the said period; and
(d) the further steps proposed to expand this initiative across the country?

(a) the specific initiatives taken for transforming the North Eastern Region (NER) into a strategic commercial and diplomatic gateway to Southeast Asia;
(b) the milestones recorded in executing key cross-border projects, notably the Kaladan Multi-Modal Transit Transport and the India-Myanmar-Thailand Trilateral Highway, to facilitate seamless integration;
(c) the status of the North East Economic Corridor and its task forces; and 
(d) the role of investment summits and North Eastern Development Finance Corporation (NEDFi) in promoting private investment, entrepreneurship and industrial growth in the North Eastern Region?

(a) the enforcement milestones of the Telecommunications Act, 2023, which replaces colonial-era laws to modernise the sector's regulatory framework;
(b) how the authorization-based regime streamlines administrative processes for providers and promotes innovation through the Regulatory Sandbox framework;
(c) the details of status of 2026 rules for principal, captive and miscellaneous services and Digital Bharat Nidhi's support for R&D, pilots and rural connectivity; and
(d) the specific measures under the Act to enhance user protection, such as mandatory consent for commercial messages and steps against cyber-financial fraud and spam?

(a) the core objectives and framework of the Divyangjan Kaushal Vikas Yojana envisioned in Union Budget 2026-27 to provide industry-aligned vocational training for Persons with Disabilities (PwDs);
(b) the strategic methodology for designing specialised training modules in high-growth sectors such as information technology, AVGC and hospitality for Divyangjan beneficiaries;
(c) whether barrier-free infrastructure and advanced assistive technologies are being successfully integrated across skilling centers identified under the scheme, if so, the details thereof; and
(d) the comprehensive initiatives implemented to ensure effective market linkages and sustainable livelihood generation for certified Divyangjan candidates?

(a) the milestones achieved under the Nasha Mukt Bharat Abhiyaan in curbing the demand for narcotics and psychotropic substances, especially among the youth demographic;
(b) the strategic framework adopted to fortify the network of Integrated Rehabilitation Centres for Addicts and promote community-based, peer-led intervention models;
(c) whether a national toll-free de-addiction helpline and specialised outreach programmes across academic institutions have been successfully operationalised;
(d) if so, the details thereof; and
(e) the specific initiatives implemented to cultivate a professional cadre of volunteers and Master Volunteers to spearhead grassroots awareness and social advocacy?

(a) the progress achieved under the "Sahakar se Samriddhi" vision in setting up new multipurpose Primary Agriculture Cooperative Credit Societies (PACS), dairy and fishery cooperative societies in previously unserved Gram Panchayats;
(b) whether the adoption of Model Bye-Laws has successfully empowered primary societies to expand their operational scope into diverse service-delivery domains;
(c) if so, the details thereof; and
(d) the specific strategies formulated to bridge regional disparities and revitalise the cooperative movement in States where its presence is relatively low?

(a) the total number of beneficiaries covered under the Pradhan Mantri Ujjwala Yojana (PMUY) as on May 2026;
(b) the progress made so far in LPG connections distribution in 2026;
(c) whether improved LPG coverage under PMUY had an impact on the reduction of respiratory diseases and health conditions related to indoor air pollution; and
(d) the safety initiatives undertaken, including free inspections and LPG hose replacement?

(a) the key features of Jal Jeevan Mission (JJM) 2.0 and the major changes that have been made in it as compared to the previous phase of the Mission;
(b) the implementation framework and funding pattern under the Mission;
(c) the reforms proposed to strengthen source sustainability, operation and maintenance of rural water supply systems and community participation;
(d) the State-wise funds allocated and released under JJM 2.0 during the year 2026-27; and
(e) the timeline and targets for achieving universal and sustainable rural household tap water supply under the Mission?

(a) progress made in implementation of First Mile Connectivity (FMC) projects, including number of projects commissioned, under implementation and proposed as on date;
(b) whether targets under the Coal Logistics Plan and Policy, 2030 have been achieved, particularly with regard to rail connectivity, mechanised coal handling and conveyor-based transportation;
(c) the bottlenecks identified in evacuation of coal from pitheads to end-use destinations, if so, the details thereof;
(d) measures taken to reduce coal logistics costs and improve evacuation efficiency through multimodal transport and dedicated rail infrastructure; and
(e) impact of these initiatives on coal dispatch and timely supply to the power plants and other consuming sectors?

(a) whether Government has approved the proposal for setting up a Greenfield airport at Doloo in Cachar district, near Silchar, Assam;
(b) if so, the present status of the project including site clearance, preparation of Detailed Project Report (DPR), land acquisition, environmental and statutory clearances;
(c) whether any timeline has been fixed for commencement and completion of construction of the said airport and, if so, the details thereof; and
(d) if not, the reasons for delay and the steps being taken by Government to expedite implementation of the Greenfield airport project in view of the strategic, economic and connectivity needs of the Barak Valley region of Assam?

(a) the infrastructure and tourism resources developed or upgraded under G20 tourism initiatives under PRASAD scheme during the last year State-wise including Tripura and Madhya Pradesh;
(b) whether the usage levels of these resources have met the prescribed standards;
(c) if so, the details thereof;
(d) whether a number of States have reported challenges in operation or maintenance;
(e) if so, the details thereof, State-wise;
(f) whether the outcome-based audits have been done for expenditure related to G20 tourism; 
(g) if so, the details thereof; and
(h) the corrective measures taken to ensure long-term tourism value, State-wise, including Tripura and Madhya Pradesh?

(a) whether Government has assessed the performance of Indian Tsunami Early Warning Centre during seismic events during the last five years;
(b) whether any system upgrades or mock drills have been conducted during this period;
(c) if so, the details thereof;
(d) the manner in which advisories are being disseminated to coastal districts and fishing communities;
(e) the improvements made in ocean State and storm-surge forecasting; and
(f) the coordination mechanisms with coastal States and maritime agencies?

(a) the Prime Minister's Development Initiative for North East Region (PM-DevINE) projects that were sanctioned and grounded during the last year, State-wise including Tripura;
(b) the physical and financial progress achieved against approved timelines;
(c) whether delays have occurred due to finalisation of Detailed Project Reports (DPRs), land acquisition or State capacity constraints;
(d) if so, the details thereof;
(e) how third-party monitoring and outcome verification are being conducted; and
(f) the corrective actions taken in under-performing projects?

(a) the major investor summits and promotional platforms organised for the North Eastern Region;
(b) the investment proposals received through these initiatives;
(c) the role of North Eastern Development Finance Corporation Ltd. (NEDFi) in financing startups and MSMEs; and
(d) the steps taken through banking and financial institutions to improve credit access, branch expansion and digital payment coverage in the region?

(a) the cultural assets, exhibitions or institutions developed or put to use under India’s post-G20 cultural heritage initiatives;
(b) the manner in which international cultural collaborations have been expanded during the said period;
(c) the funds allocated for maintenance of G20-related cultural infrastructure;
(d) the manner in which the outcomes of cultural diplomacy are being evaluated; and
(e) the long-term strategy to establish India as a global cultural hub?

(a) the number of villages identified under the Pradhan Mantri Janjatiya Unnat Gram Abhiyan for tourism development;
(b) the funds released for tribal homestays and village tourism;
(c) the measures being undertaken by the Ministry to ensure community participation;
(d) whether these initiatives are generating local employment and income opportunities; and
(e) if so, the details thereof?

(a) the current status of implementation of the PM e-Bus Sewa–Payment Security Mechanism (PSM) Scheme, including the number of electric buses deployed or operationalised so far under the Scheme;
(b) the total number of payment security support claims processed to date, the quantum of funds released from PSM;
(c) whether any instances of Public Transport Authorities (PTAs) payment defaults have been recorded;
(d) if so, the corrective measures undertaken thereof;
(e) whether the Ministry has undertaken any assessment of the operational performance, utilisation rates or service outcomes of electric buses supported under the Scheme; and
(f) if so, the key findings?

(a) the approvals granted under the second tranche of the Electronics Components Manufacturing Scheme (ECMS), including the total proposed investment and projected production values;
(b) the States in which the newly approved units are located and the extent to which the scheme supports balanced regional growth and high-skill employment generation;
(c) the categories of electronic components and sub-assemblies covered under the latest approvals and the key sectors expected to be served by these projects; and
(d) the details of the launch of India’s first generation energy-efficient edge silicon chip ARKA-GKT1?

(a) the manner in which the Pradhan Mantri Viksit Bharat Rozgar Yojana (PM VBRY) is different from the Atmanirbhar Bharat Rozgar Yojana (ABRY);
(b) the financial implications under PM VBRY;
(c) the number of jobs PM VBRY aims to create duing its implementation period; and
(d) the details of timeframe during which job creation under the PM VBRY would be eligible for incentives?

(a) the detailed response of Government to the petitions filed in Supreme Court on air pollution, health emergency and national health emergency protocols and the steps being taken to mitigate health risks arising from deteriorating air quality across major cities;
(b) whether Government proposes to issue any national-level health advisory or emergency protocol in coordination with the Ministry of Health and Family Welfare; and
(c) if so, the details thereof and if not, the reasons therefor?

(a) the latest progress made in strengthening project monitoring systems in the North Eastern Region, including the number and percentage of projects inspected and operationalised during the recent year;
(b) the details of reforms undertaken to improve real-time monitoring of projects, including the use of digital platforms such as Poorvottar Vikas Setu and the measurable outcomes of these reforms; and
(c) the number of delayed or stalled projects identified under the Ministry’s review mechanism during the last year and the action taken for foreclosure, refunds or revival of such projects?

(a) the measurable targets of the I4C and its State units set for 2025–26 regarding recovery of defrauded funds and disruption of transnational cybercrime networks;
(b) how is the Ministry using the Samanvaya Platform and its ‘Pratibimb’ module to enable real-time, cross-State coordination among police forces against inter State cyber criminals;
(c) what policy or legislative measures are being introduced to mandate instant reporting and fund-freezing protocols between telecom companies, banks and the 1930 Cybercrime Helpline; and
(d) how the Ministry is ensuring that the Cyber Crime Prevention against Women and Children (CCPWC) scheme improves conviction rates through timely, standardized forensic analysis from the new laboratories?

(a) whether Government has issued any guideline related to Work-from-Home for teachers in the event of schools being advised to suspend physical classes due to severe weather warnings such as heavy rainfall, red alerts or road flooding;
(b) if not, whether Government propose to issue guidelines for such emergency situations;
(c) the current status of implementation of safety measures such as CCTV cameras and voice-recording systems in schools across the country; and
(d) the steps taken by Central Government and States/UTs so far to ensure that the academic burden on children does not increase and early signs of stress can be identified?

(a) whether Government is aware of the shortage of NCERT textbooks, particularly in the remote regions;
(b) the steps taken or proposed by Government to ensure timely availability of NCERT textbooks for all students before the commencement of the academic session;
(c) the mechanism in place to ensure pan-India availability of NCERT textbooks; and
(d) whether any monitoring mechanism has been established to track the printing, supply and delivery of textbooks to schools, if so, details thereof?

(a) the key measures taken by Government to enhance the affordability of healthcare;
(b) whether Government has undertaken any initiatives to strengthen India’s position as a global destination for medical value tourism and if so, the details thereof;
(c) the steps being taken to improve collaboration with the healthcare industry and private sector to promote inclusive and high-quality medical infrastructure; and
(d) the measures proposed to promote traditional systems of medicine and wellness as part of India’s broader healthcare and export strategy?

(a) the target date for 100 per cent deployment of the indigenous Kavach safety system across the core network;
(b) the manner in which the Ministry is utilising AI and predictive maintenance tools to reduce signalling failures and accidents;
(c) whether a new policy has been adopted to mandate fire-resistant materials in all new passenger coaches;
(d) the manner in which the Ministry is accelerating the elimination of unmanned level crossings in high-density sections; and
(e) the manner in which rail tracks are fenced and protected across the country, the details thereof, zone-wise?

(a) the details of entities eligible for setting up, operating and maintaining electric vehicle (EV) charging stations under PM E-Drive scheme;
(b) the financial assistance and subsidy provisions including the total outlay for EV charging infrastructure proposed under the scheme;
(c) the criteria for selection of cities, towns and highways for installation of EV charging stations under the scheme including the focus on metropolitan cities, smart cities, satellite towns, State capitals; and
(d) the mechanisms and measures put in place to coordinate installation of EV charging stations and ensure effective deployment and maintenance of the infrastructure?

(a) the current status of the Silchar-Saurashtra East-West Corridor under the NHDP;
(b) the current status of work between Harangajao to Balacherra & Nerim Bungalow to Harangajao stretch of the East-West corridor and the expected timeline for completion of work in this stretch; and
(c) the expected timeline for the completion of the East-West corridor project?

(a) whether Government has completed the final location survey and Detailed Project Report (DPR) for the proposed alternative railway line from Lanka to Manarband in Assam;
(b) if so, the current status of approval and implementation of the project;
(c) whether Government has fixed any timeline for the commencement and completion of the said railway line; and
(d) the steps being taken to expedite the project, considering the strategic importance of this route for Barak Valley and its vulnerability during monsoons?
